The crypto stack has no wasm32 target.

`russh` pulls in `aws-lc-sys`, which compiles AWS-LC's C through a build script
with no wasm32-wasip2 path — so the cross-build fails in the dependency, before
reaching any of this package's own code.

This package already said so in prose: `loft.toml`'s `[wasm.bridge]` comment
reads "`--native-wasm` (wasip2) is likewise out of scope: russh/tokio do not
build against wasip2."  This file is that same statement where CI can read it,
so the claim is checked rather than merely written down.

Delete this file when `russh` can be built for wasm32 — and the gate will hold
the package to it.
